1 token = 4 character [or 0.75 words]

find tokens:
i.) 
character count= 800
top_k=4
  =>  tokens=character count / 4    # enga yen 4 naa = 1 token = 4 words
  =>  tokens = 800/4
  => tokens = 200

ii.)
top_k=4 chunks
    => top_k * tokens
    => 4 * 200
    => 800 tokens

---------------------------------------------------
RAG = Retrieval + Augmented + Generation

Retrieval: Documents la irundhu related part ah thedi edukkum.
Augmented: Andha part ah question oda serthu LLM ku kudukkum.
Generation: LLM andha info vechu answer eludhum.
“Hybrid Keyword-based RAG” artham

Keyword-based: Words match panni thedum. Meaning purinjikkadhu.
Example: “founder” nu keatta, docs la “founder” nu word irundha dhaan kidaikkum. “established by” nu irundha miss aagum.

Hybrid: Onnukku mela search method serthu use pannuradhu.

3 parts

1. TF-IDF Cosine Similarity (kb.py search())

Question um ovvoru chunk um numbers (vector) ah maathum.
Edhu romba similar nu score kudukkum.
TF-IDF = rare words ku adhiga weight, common words (“the”, “is”) ku kammi weight.
Words match mattum, meaning illa.

2. MySQL LIKE keyword search

Simple text search: WHERE text LIKE '%founder%'
Exact word irundha dhaan kidaikkum.
TF-IDF miss pannina idhu backup.

3. Local Extractive Sentence Fallback (_extractive() in rag.py)

Gemini fail aanaal use aagum.
Chunks la irundhu best sentences ah appadiye eduthu kaatum.
LLM illa, so answer ah rewrite pannadhu. Adhaan unrelated lines mix aagudhu.
-----------------------------------------------------------------
Report la ezhudha (sample paragraph): 
    “Indha chatbot oru Hybrid Keyword-based RAG 
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation) system. Admin upload panra PDF/TXT/MD
documents ah 800-character chunks ah pirichu MySQL database la store 
pannum. User oru question kettaal, TF-IDF cosine similarity and MySQL
 LIKE keyword search use panni, question ku related chunks ah thedum. 
 Andha chunks ah question oda serthu Gemini LLM ku anuppum, 
 LLM documents la irukkura info vechu mattum answer generate pannum.
 Gemini work aagalana, extractive fallback use panni, chunks la 
 irundhu best sentences ah answer ah kaattum. Answer illana 
 ‘Not available in KB’ nu sollum.”